<title>SLOVAKIA: Slovak FinMin 40-wk T-bill yield rises to 13.59 pc.</title>
<headline>Slovak FinMin 40-wk T-bill yield rises to 13.59 pc.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average yield at an auction of Slovak Finance Ministry 40-week treasury bills rose to 13.59 percent from 11.25 percent in the last successful auction of similar bills, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The ministry does not announce the amount of bills on offer at its auctions.</p>
<p> 40-week T-bills		 Dec 18	     Nov 27</p>
<p> Bids (in billion crowns)    4.720		1.835</p>
<p> Bids accepted		   4.690		1.030</p>
<p> Minimum yield (pct)	  12.90		10.50</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)	  13.59		11.249</p>
<p> Maximum yield (pct)	  14.00		11.49</p>
<p> Maturity date	    Sep 25, 1997     Sept 4, 1997</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-563-3687</p>
